# Builder dark mode

Light/dark is a **colour-only** dimension next to the device breakpoints.

## Must

- **Scope selector:** dark CSS uses `:where(.dark, .dark *):not(:where(.dark .light, .dark .light *))`. In TS use the shared `DARK_SCOPE_SELECTOR` / `isDarkScope()`; never plain `.dark .x`.
- **Dark bags hold colours only:** `styles.dark` accepts colour/shadow keys; `settings.background.dark` only the per-type colour/image keys. One bag for all breakpoints.
- **New colour key:** add it to the Style controls, the backend colour-key list, **and** the frontend base colour keys so it gets a dark override.
- **Widget defaults:** a Style-tab colour reads `var(--s-<key>, var(--xx-d-*))` with light/dark defaults in the widget CSS. Don't hard-code Tailwind `dark:text-*` / `dark:bg-*` for those colours — they beat the Style value.
- **Values:** hex, `rgb()/rgba()`, `var(--kit-color-[a-z0-9_-]{1,40})`, or `theme` (dark only). Validate on the backend **and** with the shared safe-colour check before writing any `<style>` text.
- **Kit colours:** pickers for Style/background colour keys allow global kit colours; hex-only fields (widget settings, particles/rain, shape dividers, the design kit itself) don't.

## Don't

- Add per-breakpoint dark values or dark sizes/spacing.
- Store theme toggles in settings — the canvas theme is editor state only.
- Inject unvalidated colour strings into CSS.
